Charles arranged games for the gathering. The qualification rules for each game are very diverse. Each game contains n rounds. If a player's highest point exceeds the total of all other points, he or she qualifies for the next round. If the player's highest point is less than or equal to the total of all other points, he or she does not qualify for the next round. Write a Java application to assist Charles in determining if the individual is eligible for the next game.For example, if a player plays a game that has 4 rounds with points 4, 3, 2, and 10, then, the player qualifies for the next round because 10 > 9 (4 + 3 + 2).Constraints:If the value of the rounds
is less than or equal to zero, print "Rounds cannot be <value>". If the player is qualified, print "Congratulations you have qualified with a maximum point <maximumPoint>". If the player is not qualified, print "Sorry you
are not qualified".Assume that points are positive and greater than zero.Note:Do not edit the existing code template.In the Sample Input / Output provided, the highlighted text in bold corresponds to the input given by the user, and the rest of the text represents the output.Implement the business requirements within the main method. Please do not change the class name.Please do not use System.exit(0); to terminate the program.



